# fi15-fi16-stardreamer-pause.drv - Stardreamer time ladder, then pause and resume.
#
# Verifies: FI-15 (Shift+F1..F5 set 1x/10x/100x/1000x/10000x while docked),
#           FI-16 (Esc stops the clock; Shift+F1 starts it again), S14 (short
#           form: screen clock only; S14's check of 10428(a6)/14482(a6) needs
#           a memory probe and stays open).
# Keys are `sdlkey` steps, so Shift+Fn goes through the port's keymap exactly
# as a Mac keyboard event with the Shift modifier would (fn-key settings of a
# real Mac keyboard are outside this test: U-07).
# Evidence: the panel clock (top left of the control panel) in each shot.
# Run:  python3 tools/drive/drive.py --script tools/drive/scripts/fi15-fi16-stardreamer-pause.drv \
#           --out RUN_DIR --timeout 90
# Expect: exit 0; the clock gains ~3 s between 01 and 02, more per 3 s at each
#         rung, is frozen between 08 and 09, and runs again in 10.

wait 6000
key space
wait 2000
key 3
wait 11000
shot 01-1x-a
wait 3000
shot 02-1x-b
sdlkey f2 shift
wait 3000
shot 03-shift-f2
sdlkey f3 shift
wait 3000
shot 04-shift-f3
sdlkey f4 shift
wait 3000
shot 05-shift-f4
sdlkey f5 shift
wait 3000
shot 06-shift-f5
sdlkey f1 shift
wait 2000
shot 07-shift-f1
sdlkey esc
wait 500
shot 08-esc-paused-a
wait 3000
shot 09-esc-paused-b
sdlkey f1 shift
wait 3000
shot 10-shift-f1-resumed
quit
